WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.320
(dramatic music)

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.030
- [Female Narrator] Robert
Johnson is considered

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.070
one of the greatest blues
artists of all time.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.200
- [Male Narrator] It's the template

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.700
for what become rock and roll.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.010
- [Male] I believe Robert
Johnson was extremely talented,

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:18.180
extremely gifted, and way off balance.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.873
Something's spinning
strangely in that man's life.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.900
Robert was a novice guitar
player, not very good.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.750
- [Man] This man was a nobody.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.940
And then he disappears.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.190
A year and a half later, he's
doing things with a guitar

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.783
that even his mentors can't do.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.700
- [Narrator] How could
Robert possibly have gotten

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.502
that good that fast?

00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:45.720
(dramatic music)

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.120
- [Male Narrator] The
myth goes that Robert

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.140
went to the crossroads,
got down on his knees,

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:52.400
handed his guitar to the devil.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.160
The devil said, once you
receive the guitar back,

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.440
your soul is mine.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.540
- [Man] If you do make
a deal with the devil,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.880
you're gonna have to pay the price.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.113
- [Narrator] It ended up costing
him, the bill coming due.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.140
- [Male] He let his arrogance go too far.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.530
- [Guy] We all have to choose

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.783
how much we can sacrifice in
order to achieve greatness.

00:01:17.135 --> 00:01:20.302
(blues guitar music)

